  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Heritage Conservation and Transmission: Strengthening Suzhou&#x2019;s Gardens and Traditional Architecture Conservation through Global Exchange</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project, led by UNESCO and WHITRAP Suzhou, strengthens the safeguarding of Suzhou&#x2019;s renowned gardens, traditional architecture, and artisanal skills through global exchange and youth engagement. It responds to challenges such as declining traditional craftsmanship, limited youth participation, and the need for innovative, sustainable conservation approaches. Over three years, the project will connect young people and heritage professionals across Asia-Pacific through innovation calls, exhibitions, symposia, and international exchanges, fostering cross-cultural learning and promoting Suzhou as a model for heritage-based sustainable development.</narrative>
  </description>
